    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d982">

                <pb facs="1145" n="949" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg949"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.515/7–1745: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 982<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Kennan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">u. s. urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-17T19:00:00-04:00">July 17, 1945—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1629. British have now agreed to proposal outlined Deptstel 1316 June 15.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d982-f1"/> Spanish
                    situation urgent. Reurtel 2570 July
                        14<anchor n="2" xml:id="d982-f2"/> inform Soviet we assume their concurrence
                    in view of reports from Ankara and Stockholm that Soviet has so warned Turks and
                    Swedes. Make point 5 of Depstel 1534 July
                        6<anchor n="3" xml:id="d982-f3"/> if can conveniently do so. For your
                    information Dept proposes to continue stressing
                    coordinated action and maintenance of trusteeship principle. This would preclude
                    particular occupying power from disposing of German external assets to its own
                    advantage. American expressions to Soviet regarding German Legation property
                    Stockholm and German shares Rumanian oil companies will probably make these
                    points.</p>
                <p>Sent to Moscow, repeated to SecState Berlin
                    for Collado and Despres.</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        C[ovey] T. O[liver]
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
